title: Silvopasture
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Silvopasture is a type of [[Regenerative]] Agriculture where animal grazing is directly mixed with other agricultural forms. Often involves tree crops, grazing crops, inter-cropping and permaculture, all with animal raising.

Silvopasture integrates trees, pasture, and livestock into a single system, promoting ecological interactions and synergies between trees, understory plants, soil, and animals. This approach enhances biodiversity, improves soil health, and increases carbon sequestration, while also providing economic benefits through diversified farm products like timber, livestock, and fruits.

One of [[Project Drawdown's|Drawdown.org]] top 100 solutions.